Grid (contact-sheet) mode for splay — a full-viewport thumbnail grid and the browsing/navigation around it.

The headline deliverable is a full-viewport thumbnail grid for finding frames in large sequences: an N×M page over the current scope, cursor navigation, click/Enter to open, Esc to cancel — reusing splay's existing `thumb()` cache and per-draw budget so the first draw stays responsive on big sets. A browsing/navigation strand, distinct from its two siblings: [[splay-graticule]] owns the `.reg` overlay engine, [[splay-mosaics]] owns raw-Bayer / heat-map inspection and general viewer features. Grid mode is pure browsing UI — no overlay, no pixel processing: if a change is about *finding your way around a sequence*, it's this strand. All code lands in `~/splay` (development in the `splay-grid-mode` worktree); this dir holds only curation.
